NAME
    ssh-askpass - OpenSSH askpass companion for ssh.lib.sh

SYNOPSIS
    ssh-askpass prompt

DESCRIPTION
    ssh-askpass is the bootstrap-integrated helper used by ssh_auth and
    ssh_password.

    OpenSSH invokes the helper with one prompt operand.

    In ssh_auth mode, the helper reads one record from the private repeatable
    FIFO identified by m_SSH_ASKPASS_FIFO. Each secret-entry invocation may
    therefore receive the same caller-owned secret.

    In ssh_password mode, the helper consumes the invocation-owned one-shot IPC
    value identified by m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID.

    When OpenSSH marks the request as a confirmation prompt through
    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT=confirm, ssh-askpass refuses the request before consuming
    authentication data.

    The two transport identities are mutually exclusive. Normal callers use
    ssh_auth or ssh_password from ssh.lib.sh rather than invoking this command
    directly.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_FIFO
        Absolute private FIFO pathname established by ssh_auth for repeatable
        secret delivery.

    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID
        One-shot IPC identity established by ssh_password.

    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT
        OpenSSH prompt classification. The value confirm is refused.

EXIT STATUS
    0   authentication value delivered successfully
    1   confirmation request, invalid/missing transport identity, conflicting
        transport identities, or transport failure
    2   invocation does not contain exactly one prompt operand

SEE ALSO
    ssh.lib.sh
    ipc.lib.sh
